```console
$ caliper-docgen extract --help
Extract prop types and write to stdout or --out file

Usage: caliper-docgen extract [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -s, --src <SRC>
          Source directories to scan [default: ./src]

  -o, --out <OUT>
          Output file [default: stdout]

  -f, --format <FORMAT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - canonical: caliper-docgen canonical schema (richest)
          - rdt:       react-docgen-typescript compatible output
          - storybook: Storybook __docgenInfo blocks
          - toon:      Token-Optimized Object Notation (compact agent format)
          
          [default: canonical]

      --cache-dir <CACHE_DIR>
          Cache directory

      --html-attributes <HTML_ATTRIBUTES>
          How much of an inherited HTML element's attributes to expose

          Possible values:
          - curated: ~15-20 curated, commonly-documented attributes per element
            (default)
          - full:    All of `@types/react`'s real attributes for the element
            (matches RDT)
          - none:    No inherited HTML attributes at all — own props only

      --extra-builtins <EXTRA_BUILTINS>
          Extra type names to treat as recognized/builtin (no "unknown type"
          warning) — e.g. a library-specific type this tool doesn't already know

  -j, --json
          Machine-readable JSON output: the canonical schema, compact, always to
          stdout, ignoring --out/--format (which govern the human/RDT/Storybook
          paths below), and suppresses the human-readable summary/diagnostics

      --load-dependencies
          Load the type declarations props reference from installed packages
          (off by default)

  -v, --verbose...
          Verbose output (repeat for more: -v, -vv)

      --collapse-inherited-props <COLLAPSE_INHERITED_PROPS>
          Which inherited sources of more than 30 props to list as one inherited
          layer instead of prop by prop

          Possible values:
          - dependencies: Sources from loaded dependencies (default)
          - all:          Dependency and project sources
          - none:         List every prop

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress all non-error output

      --config <CONFIG>
          Path to docgen.config.ts

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

```
